WEBVTT

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:06.350
Three tricky moments when you talk about decisions.

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:10.030
Moment one: “But you’re the manager, you decide.”

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:14.550
Some teams expect you to decide everything, and some managers like that.

00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:17.930
But it makes you a bottleneck, and the team stops thinking.

00:00:17.980 --> 00:00:21.870
Be clear about which decisions you keep, and which you hand over.

00:00:21.920 --> 00:00:24.030
Then really hand them over.

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:28.730
If you overrule a delegated decision once, people will stop believing you.

00:00:28.780 --> 00:00:33.850
Moment two: everyone wants consensus for everything. It feels fair.

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:40.610
In practice it means the slowest, most cautious person decides, and big decisions drag on for weeks.

00:00:40.660 --> 00:00:46.190
Introduce consent as an alternative: “Is this good enough for now, and safe enough to try?”

00:00:46.240 --> 00:00:50.250
It keeps everyone’s voice, without needing everyone’s first choice.

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:53.890
Moment three: the decision is not yours to give.

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:59.790
Some decisions belong to people outside the team: your manager, another department, a steering group.

00:00:59.840 --> 00:01:01.550
Don’t pretend otherwise.

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:04.770
Write them on the canvas too, with the real owner.

00:01:04.820 --> 00:01:09.870
It’s useful for the team to see where their influence ends, and where they can still give input.

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:11.850
And a tip for after the session.

00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:14.150
Write decisions down when you make them.

00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:23.210
A simple decision log, with the date, what was decided, by whom and why, ends a lot of “who decided this?” conversations before they start.

00:01:23.260 --> 00:01:26.170
If someone wants to reopen a decision, that’s allowed.

00:01:26.220 --> 00:01:28.970
But ask: “What new information do we have?”

00:01:29.020 --> 00:01:31.046
If there isn’t any, the decision stands.

